{
  "about": "Golden vectors for repairing a Plex response that holds bytes that are not UTF-8. Read by BOTH Nostalgex/NostalgexTests/PlexUTF8RepairGoldenTests.swift (PlexUTF8Repair, the Apple TV) and scripts/nostalgex-utf8-repair-smoke.mjs (the web tuner, npm run test:utf8-repair). Each case gives the input bytes as hex, the text they must decode to, and how many bytes were repaired (0 means the input is valid UTF-8 and is decoded untouched). The rule: every byte outside a well-formed UTF-8 sequence (Unicode table 3-7) is read as Windows-1252, the five bytes that table leaves undefined keep their Latin-1 code point. When the rule changes, change both engines, then update or add a case here. A leading byte order mark is not covered: the web drops it, as Response.json() does.",
